    "rRNA": {
      "description": "A nuclear ribosomal RNA locus that GENCODE types rRNA and that MGI does not mark as a pseudogene. Every member is 5S- or 5.8S-sized: 170 predicted Gm* gene models, 180 n-R5s* copies of the 5S repeat, and the named Rn5s and n-R5-8s1 loci. There is no 18S, 28S or 45S gene model in this category, because the mouse rDNA arrays are not represented in the mm10 primary assembly.",
      "source": "The gene_type attribute of the GENCODE M25 GTF, minus the two loci moved to rRNA_pseudogene below on MGI's authority (MGI MRK_List2.rpt, retrieved 2026-08-22, joined through the mgi_id attribute the GTF itself carries). Read the count before you use it: this category holds 352 loci, of which 170 are predicted Gm* models and 180 are copies of the 5S repeat, whereas the human files in this set ship 29 on hg38 and 19 on hg19. That gap is a real difference between the two annotations and not something this package can fix, because GENCODE never applies the rRNA_pseudogene biotype to mouse at all, so the ~500 rRNA-derived loci that human splits off as pseudogenes stay inside mouse rRNA. An rRNA fraction computed from this category is therefore not comparable to one computed from the human files unless the caller first decides which of these loci should count. Nor is it comparable across mouse releases by id: vM25 and vM39 annotate the same 356 loci, but only 14 of them keep their gene id and only 83 keep their gene name, so this list must be read for the release it names.",
